  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations for HUBZone set-asides total $393M across 1,171 awards, with an average award size of $336K. These are fiscal year to date figures and therefore partial. Obligations were down 57.3% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a clear fall from prior peak years: FY23 was $1.1B, FY22 was $1B, and FY21 was $938M. FY25 obligations were $920M and FY24 was $1B. The Department of Defense leads buying with $137M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $64.3M and the Department of Labor at $51.2M. At the vendor level, T&H SERVICES, LLC is the largest recipient at $22.8M, followed by PANAMERICA COMPUTERS, INC. at $19.2M and FEDERAL RESOURCES CORPORATION at $17.2M. By industry, Other Computer Related Services accounts for $108M of obligations, Other Technical and Trade Schools accounts for $41.5M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $38M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations are $393M, a drop from recent years where FY23 reached $1.1B and FY22 and FY24 each reached $1B. FY25 obligations were $920M and FY21 was $938M. Overall, obligations were down 57.3% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are driving FY2026 to date obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency at $137M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $64.3M and the Department of Labor at $51.2M. Other Computer Related Services leads industries at $108M, with Other Technical and Trade Schools at $41.5M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $38M."
      }
    ]
  },
